# Chaos: no quiver by hard-coded id (client/BASE.md "0173"; src/client/item.cpp; after 0001-0172).
# Item::isQuiver named eight client ids (35524, 35562, 35848, 35849, 36666, 39150, 39160, 45644) and getItem reads a count
# byte for a quiver. In our pair those ids are plain decoration (server 38524, 38562, 38848, 38849, 43150, 43160 are not
# stackable, so the server writes no count byte): the client read one byte too many, threw, and dropped the rest of that
# server message (a tile or map packet with such an item in it; a creature removal after it stayed unprocessed: a dead
# monster stayed drawn, 2026-10-30). A quiver is now what the item type says (weapon type quiver) or what the dat's market
# category says (category 25), nothing else. server/tools/check_item_wire.py has the same rule.
diff -ruN a/src/client/item.cpp b/src/client/item.cpp
